// REJECTS: Unexpected token 'name'. Valid alternatives: ['host', 'port', 'serviceName']
//
// `name:` on an Oracle specification. Oracle is a four-token grammar -- Oracle, host, port,
// serviceName -- and it has no NAME token at all: the database is addressed by `serviceName`,
// which is Oracle's own concept and not a rename of anything.
//
// This is the same class of divergence as ./neg-databricks-host-not-hostname.pure and worth
// pinning separately because it fails in the other direction: there, a universal field name
// was missing from one vendor; here, the vendor uses a word no other vendor in the batch has,
// while `name` -- which Aurora, Redshift and Static all accept -- is absent. The two together
// bracket the assumption that these specs are one schema with optional fields.
//
// The alternative list is the complete Oracle datasource surface.
###Connection
RelationalDatabaseConnection fixture::neg::OracleName
{
  store: fixture::neg::Db;
  type: Oracle;
  specification: Oracle
  {
    name: 'name';
    host: 'host';
    port: 1234;
  };
  auth: Test;
}
